  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "Validation was limited to selected areas within two European cities, which may not capture the full diversity of global sidewalk conditions or image coverage gaps.",
      "what": "The authors created the Wheelchair Accessibility Dataset pipeline, which processes Mapillary street-level imagery using monocular metric depth estimation, 3D point cloud reconstruction, and terrain models to measure sidewalk segmentation, surface condition, clearance, and slope. These measurements generate the Wheelchair Accessibility Index (WHAI), which was validated using aerial orthoimagery and unmanned aerial vehicle data across test locations in Łódź, Poland, and Heidelberg, Germany.",
      "why": "This approach converts publicly available street images into granular 3D infrastructure metrics, allowing planners to detect micro-level physical barriers and inaccessible urban enclaves that standard network analyses miss."
    }
  },
